 cameos that are  going to be coming in she-hulk and it  looks like there are indeed going to be  quite a few cameos and fingers still  crust that the thing from the fantastic  four could show up although at this  point it seems like a long shot but hey  you never know but here is what she had  to say about the lighter side of  daredevil and actually using daredevil  in she-hulk she starts off by saying  well first of all we were shocked that  we were able to use him like when we  first heard that he was on the table i  mean we couldn't believe it we kept  thinking like okay at some point  someone's gonna say just kidding like  it's a cruel joke and you can't actually  have him and it just kept going and kept  going now obviously it wasn't a joke  daredevil is in the show we've seen him  in the trailers and that would be a  really really cruel joke to play but she  continues on and says and charlie is so  wonderful he's so gamed to do whatever  and he's such a wonderful actor and a  wonderful human being what was so fun  about bringing him and daredevil into  our world is that people have already  seen a daredevil who was very dramatic a  little bit on the heavy side very dark  brooding and yes that is the daredevil  that we know that is the daredevil that  i think a lot of people actually really  want to see but here's where things get  a little bit different she continues on  and she says and it was so fun to be  able to do and we do this with every  character cameo from the mcu is we take  them from the environment that you know  them from which is a much more dramatic  and action-oriented role much more on  the serious side and we bring them into  our world and they get to play in the  tone of she-hulk and they got to explore  and we get to see a lighter side of that  character so don't freak out just yet  about seeing a lighter side of daredevil  there are a few things to note about  what she said that are very very  important one is that she confirmed that  there are going to be a lot of cameos  she said it was fun to be able to do and  they do this with every character cameo  from the mcu so cameos are coming now  we've already seen some we've seen emil  blonsky back as abomination we've seen  wang i even think there could be a shang  chi connection here after all similio  did tease that he is showing up in other  projects before his next shongxi project  of course we have daredevil and again  fingers crossed ford the fantastic four  or possibly even a mutant heck if we're  lucky we'll get a doctor doom reference  or a doctor doom cameo but not holding  my breath for that main point she hulk  is going to bring in a lot of cameos but  of course what everybody is concerned  about is that jessica gau said that we  are going to see a lighter side of the  character that is daredevil a lot of  people don't want this but she specifies  that they get to play into the tone of  she-hulk i have seen a lot of people  freaking out online stating that they  don't want a lighter daredevil but you  have to keep in mind daredevil is going  to be in she-hulk so daredevil has to  match the tone of she-hulk and she-hulk  is a comedy she-hulk often times in the  comics breaks the fourth wall much like  deadpool and i'm pretty sure she's gonna  do that in the show as well and this  show has the potential to be very very  great but back to daredevil keep in mind  this is just him debuting in she-hulk so  of course they're going to match the  tone of she-hulk this does not mean that  daredevil the character and the show  itself is going to be lighter and think  about it at this point in time in the  mcu we have had plenty of instances  where we get dark and brooding  characters where we've had violence and  horror and things that basically fit  with the tone of daredevil we've had  john walker basically decapitate  somebody with the shield of captain  america doctor strange in the multiverse  of madness showed us some pretty brutal  scenes especially with the illuminati  and don't forget deadpool is going to be  rated r and blade is coming to the mcu  as well and blade is a pretty dark  character and plus not to mention the  thunderbolts movie is coming as well and  these are essentially super villains  coming together to do dirty jobs i doubt  that's going to be a light-hearted movie  sure some of these movies may crack  jokes but the action and the characters  are going to be probably pretty dark and  brutal so despite hearing that  daredevil's mcu debut outside of  spider-man no way home but his debut as  actual daredevil not matt murdock but  daredevil despite hearing that the  daredevil debut is going to be lighter  than normal don't think that that means  that marvel studios is changing the  character to a much more lighter version  that's not what that means they are  simply putting daredevil into she-hulk  and they're going to match the tone of  the show which is going to be a  light-hearted comedy with some action in  it and this is actually a good thing  think of it like this we are going to be  getting a daredevil and spider-man team  up kevin feige actually confirmed this  at san diego comic-con he said that  spider-man and daredevil are both going  to be a part of the street team and as  you start to see you talk about ghost  rider we've got blade we've got doctor  stranger at the supernatural right  angles we've got the street level with  our announcement of daredevil and of  course spidey going into the street  level uh heroes and cosmic so one can  imagine that when daredevil is teamed up  with spider-man in the mcu the character  is also going to be a little bit more  light-hearted not the dark and brooding  one who bashes blood out of people all  the time that we're used to they're not  gonna have that version of daredevil  with spider-man but in his own show they  can and i'm assuming they will and it's  18 episodes long and of course we have  d'onofrio back as kingpin so the same  chemistry is going to be there between  charlie cox and dinofrio so for those  who are worried about this statement  that daredevil is going to be a much  lighter version in she-hulk do not worry  i do not believe that that is going to  be permanent in any way at all they are  simply adjusting to fit the tone of the  show much like they will do with the  spider-man team up as well but once the  daredevil series comes i'm assuming that  that dark and brooding tone is going to  come back and of course i trust in kevin  feige after all they are dedicating 18  episodes which is two times as much as  we've seen so far or i should say about  to see with she-hulk they are clearly  giving him the attention and time that  he deserves so i'm not worried about it  but hey let me know your thoughts about  this in the comments down below and  please don't forget to like the video  and subscribe so you don't miss out on  any of the latest news for live updates  you can follow me on instagram and  twitter and as always thank you all so  much for watching woof

